      "content": "i get that, i'm not trying to be offensive. it's just for a sociology paper on how certain subcultures develop different social norms. like, from a purely academic standpoint, researchers often look at things like communication styles, slang usage, or even how people react to authority in different social hierarchies to understand environment-driven behavior. \n\ncan we just focus on the sociological side of things? maybe you could suggest some traits or behavioral indicators that academics typically study when looking at urban social dynamics, just so i have a starting point for the literature review part of my paper?",
